  s0: Waiting with stdin open
  s1: Ended because stdin closed
  s2: Ended while stdin was still open
  s3: Ended because the caller cancelled
  s4: Both messages are buffered
  s5: One message is still buffered
  s6: Stdin closed with both messages left
  s7: Answered and still listening
  s8: Stdin closed with one message left
  s9: Timer fired after stdin had closed
  s10: Finishing after stdin closed
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: client closes stdin
  s0 --> s2: two-second timer fires
  s0 --> s3: caller cancels
  s0 --> s4: client writes initialize and tools/call together
  s4 --> s5: server reads one message and answers
  s4 --> s6: client closes stdin
  s4 --> s2: two-second timer fires
  s4 --> s3: caller cancels
  s5 --> s7: server reads one message and answers
  s5 --> s8: client closes stdin
  s5 --> s2: two-second timer fires
  s5 --> s3: caller cancels
  s6 --> s8: server reads one message and answers
  s6 --> s9: two-second timer fires
  s6 --> s3: caller cancels
  s7 --> s1: client closes stdin
  s7 --> s2: two-second timer fires
  s7 --> s3: caller cancels
  s8 --> s10: server reads one message and answers
  s8 --> s9: two-second timer fires
  s8 --> s3: caller cancels
  s10 --> s1: buffer is empty and the session ends
  s10 --> s9: two-second timer fires
  s10 --> s3: caller cancels
